OL,3,AFed has 'work to do' if price rises
OL,4,Adon't ease for Americans, Warsh says
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe head of the US central bank said
OL,7,Fpolicymakers will "have work to do" if
OL,8,Fthey are not confident cost of living
OL,9,Fpressures are easing for Americans.
OL,11,FFederal Reserve chairman Kevin Warsh
OL,12,Fsaid while inflation readings looked
OL,13,Fbetter than expected over the summer,
OL,14,Fthey did not show that the current
OL,15,Fpicture had "meaningfully improved".
OL,17,FThe new Fed boss stressed that his
OL,18,Fremarks should not be treated as a
OL,19,Fguide for future interest rate
OL,20,Fdecisions, but the comments suggest
OL,21,Frates could be raised if policymakers
OL,22,Fbelieve inflation is too high.
OL,23,APub: 28-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
